      {
        "title": "Baby Language Milestones 0 to 12 months: Cooing, Laughing, and Mo",
        "url": "https://www.healthline.com/health/baby/language-milestones-0-to-12-months",
        "description": "He may respond to his name, and be able to tell the difference between happy and angry tones of voice. <strong>Your baby will be able to express happiness by giggling or cooing</strong>, and unhappiness by crying, and he will continue to learn.",
        "position": 1
      },
      {
        "title": "Cooing in Babies: Meaning, Milestones & How to Encourage It - Blueberry Pediatrics",
        "url": "https://www.blueberrypediatrics.com/health-tips/understanding-cooing-in-infants-a-pediatricians-guide-for-parents",
        "description": "The CDC includes “makes sounds other than crying” as a 2-month milestone. By 4 months, babies should be making cooing sounds like “ooh” and “aah.” · Frequent cooing is a great sign! It means your baby is happy, engaged, and practicing their communication skills. Babies who get lots of face-to-face interaction tend to coo more. Some babies may start making very early cooing sounds as young as 4 to 6 weeks.",
        "position": 2
      },
      {
        "title": "Baby Language Development: 1–3 months | Nemours KidsHealth",
        "url": "https://kidshealth.org/en/parents/c13m.html",
        "description": "When do babies start cooing? <strong>Around 1–3-months</strong>. They also use expressions like smiling, crying, and laughing.",
        "position": 3
      },
      {
        "title": "What Are Baby Developmental Milestones?",
        "url": "https://my.clevelandclinic.org/health/articles/22063-baby-development-milestones-safety",
        "description": "Language and communication milestones: <strong>How your baby makes sounds and uses nonverbal communication</strong> (like “cooing” or raising their arms so you’ll pick them up) Cognitive milestones: How your baby thinks, learns and solves problems (like ...",
        "position": 4
      },
      {
        "title": "Language development: Speech milestones for babies - Mayo Clinic",
        "url": "https://www.mayoclinic.org/healthy-lifestyle/infant-and-toddler-health/in-depth/language-development/art-20045163",
        "description": "Markers, known as milestones, can be a guide to how well a child is learning to talk. These milestones help healthcare professionals know when a child might need some help. ... <strong>Smile when you show up</strong>. Make cooing sounds.",
        "position": 5
      }
    ]
  }
}

